				<dd><a href="/lsc/asset/areaguide/area02-010.jpg" data-pswp-width="1280" data-pswp-height="800"><img src="/lsc/asset/areaguide/area02-010.jpg" alt="Kobe Municipal Arboretum" width="100" height="100" loading="lazy"></a></dd>
			</dl>
		</div>
		<section class="areaInfo">
			<h3 class="areaCatch">A hotspot for mountaintop views and outdoor activities</h3>
			<div class="areaText">
				<p>
					Mt. Maya and Mt. Rokko are part of the mountain range that surrounds Kobe city from the west to the north. Rising to 931 meters, Mt. Rokko has an amazing number of recreational facilities in a natural setting.<br>
					Rokko Garden Terrace is the place to enjoy a grand panorama from the observation deck, as well as seasonal gourmet food and shopping. Kikuseidai, the observation platform on Mt. Maya, is not to be missed either. The night views of Kobe city and Osaka Bay in particular are breathtaking and count as one of Japan’s three great night views.<br>
					The Rokko mountain range also has over 70 trekking trails for all levels of ability and experience, with cable cars and ropeways making them easily accessible. 
				</p>
			</div>
			<figure class="areaPhoto"><img src="/lsc/asset/areaguide/area02-003.jpg" alt="Rokko-Shidare Observatory" width="100" height="100"></figure>
		</section>
