		<section class="areaInfo">
			<h3 class="areaCatch">Within walking distance of Shin-Kobe shinkansen station is an exotic neighborhood and an urban oasis</h3>
			<div class="areaText">
				<p>
					A short distance to the north of Sannomiya Station, downtown Kobe, is Kitano, where Ijinkan (foreigner residences) dating from the late 19th century line the streets. Wandering is well rewarded, but this is a great place to go to enjoy sophisticated relaxation, be it to enjoy a photo shoot in period costume or to sit back in the café inside a renovated mansion.<br>
					A quick step away from Shin-Kobe station also reveals an oasis of calm, a herb garden and pristine waterfalls free of city noise, highly popular with visitors from Japan and around the world.
				</p>
			</div>
			<figure class="areaPhoto"><img src="/lsc/asset/areaguide/area04-004.jpg" alt="Nunobiki Falls" width="100" height="100"></figure>
		</section>
